---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import NavBar from '../components/NavBar.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Roadmap" description="amber roadmap — what's coming next">
  <NavBar />
  <main>
    <h1>Roadmap</h1>

    <section class="section">
      <p>
        amber is a bare-metal C++ agent harness. The roadmap is about expanding what
        the harness can do, not about adding more UI polish.
      </p>
    </section>

    <hr class="divider-thick" />

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Near Term</h2>
      <ul class="feature-list">
        <li>Long-duration research projects — tmux integration, days/weeks of autonomous work</li>
        <li>Semantic search backends — real embedding models for code search</li>
        <li>Plugin system expansion — more tool types, more search modes</li>
        <li>Cross-platform considerations — Windows WSL, macOS support</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <hr class="divider" />

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Mid Term</h2>
      <ul class="feature-list">
        <li>Multi-agent orchestration — sub-agents with shared context, parallel execution</li>
        <li>Advanced compression — selective pruning, context-aware summarization</li>
        <li>Better MCP transport — full stdio and HTTP support with lifecycle management</li>
        <li>Real-time collaboration — multiple users on the same agent instance</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <hr class="divider" />

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Far Term</h2>
      <ul class="feature-list">
        <li>Self-hosted LLM support — local inference, quantized models, VRAM management</li>
        <li>Distributed agent clusters — multiple agents working on the same project</li>
        <li>Custom model training — fine-tuning on project-specific data</li>
        <li>Web UI — browser-based access to the terminal agent</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <hr class="divider" />

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Not on the Roadmap</h2>
      <p>Some things amber is not going to do:</p>
      <ul class="feature-list">
        <li>Python bindings — amber is C++, not a Python wrapper</li>
        <li>Mobile apps — terminal-native, not mobile-native</li>
        <li>Chatbot interfaces — amber is an agent harness, not a chat UI</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
